      "crowdsourced_ai_results": [
        {
          "analysis": "The binary is an ARM-based botnet client, likely a variant of the Yakuza botnet, as indicated by strings like \"[ Yakuza ] Result\". It connects to a command-and-control (C2) server, announced by a \"[BOT JOINED]\" message. Its primary capabilities include launching various DDoS attacks (TCP, UDP, HTTP floods) and self-propagation. The propagation is handled by a Telnet scanner (`TelnetScanner` function) that bruteforces credentials on port 23 and, upon success, reports the credentials and attempts to infect the new victim. The malware also features a downloader functionality, observed in the `SendWGET` function and the IOC URL `http://147[.]135[.]248[.]108/bins.sh;`.",
          "source": "palm",
